{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791572143,"nonce":"HZ6Ov1hDO5bRjck0SVx1rrbQTZ8=","title":"Host-run effects for both SDKs: ids instead of closures","message":"blinc_core 0e4ffada adds effects with no Rust closure (create_host_effect), a pull of due effect ids (take_due_host_effects) and a tracking scope for host code (begin_effect/end_effect on a graph a context owns, begin_host_effect/end_host_effect on the global graph), and makes subscribing and disposing linear in a signal's subscribers (Blinc git-bugs 1b04867, 3a01259).\n\n**Here**\n- GraphContext (owned, for blinc_ts): host effects by key, due ids, and the scope, with its deferred commands drained at the outermost end (blinc_ts git-bug d41ba78).\n- The HashLink exports (for ashui): make and release a host effect, take due ids into a buffer, begin and end (ashui git-bug 26eb780).\nEach effect then costs the SDK an id, not a GC root or N-API reference and a boxed closure, and the host runs due effects in one pass.","files":null}]}